>> title: Sourdough Loaf
>> servings: 1 loaf
>> source: Cooking wiki

Feed @sourdough starter{100%g} the night before and leave it somewhere warm for about ~{8%hours} -- it wants to be at its peak, not past it.

Mix @strong white flour{450%g} with @water{330%g} in a #large bowl{} and leave to autolyse for ~{40%minutes}.

Add the starter and @salt{9%g}, then fold in the bowl every ~{30%minutes} for the first ~{2%hours}.

Shape, put in a #banneton{}, and prove in the fridge overnight for ~{12%hours}.

Bake in a #dutch oven{} at 250C, lid on, for ~{20%minutes}, then lid off at 220C for another ~{20%minutes}.

-- The starter half of this is on [[alice.test/cooking::Sourdough Starter@2026-09-01|its own page]]; this file is only the loaf.
